WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.400
How much electricity does this one line of code use?

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:15.300
One million requests a day, for a year:
41 kg CO₂e from this single line.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:22.900
Data-centre electricity use more than doubles in six years:
415 TWh (2024) → ~945 TWh (2030). Source: IEA.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.300
Yeşil Kod (“Green Code”): measures, fixes, proves.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:39.800
Yeşil Kod found the waste and rewrote the line itself.
The 2,000-row output is identical.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:52.300
The same 62 requests, two versions, measured live.
465× less energy, same result.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:01:01.800
Four real-world wastes. The engine fixed all four.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:09.300
Find · Fix · Verify · Measure.
A working Python prototype: CLI, live panel, report on every change.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.000
You can’t optimise what you don’t measure.
Try your own code at the stand.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:24.000
Scan to try your own Python code on your phone.
